  "chapter": 732,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 58 Chapter 732\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4266-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to establish a task force on missing women and girls who are\n        black,  indigenous  and  people  of color; and providing for the\n        repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill establishes a task force on missing women and girls who  are\nBlack, Indigenous and People of Color (\"BIPOC\") that will study and make\npolicy recommendations to address the lack of care and concern for miss-\ning and murdered BIPOC women and girls.\n \n  I fully support the goals of this bill, which would shine a much-need-\ned  light  on cases of missing BIPOC women and girls and develop strate-\ngies for advancing the safety  of  this  population.  Too  often,  cases\ninvolving  missing  or  murdered BIPOC women and girls are overlooked or\nhandled without adequate care. The tens of thousands  of  missing  BIPOC\nwomen  in  the United States include abductees, sex trafficking victims,\nand runaways. These individuals experience the  intersection  of  racism\nand sexism, which results in pervasive social and economic barriers. The\nState  must  do everything in its power to prevent BIPOC women and girls\nfrom being harmed and to help ensure the safety of and bring justice for\nthose who are still missing.\n \n  Creating a commission, study, or task force is a process  best  suited\nfor  the  budget  process, due to the fiscal costs of these entities. As\nthe Legislature set aside funding in the FY24 Enacted  Budget  for  this\ninitiative,  I  fully  support  empaneling  this task force through this\nbill.  However, technical changes are necessary to ensure the task force\ncould be implemented in a fiscally responsible way.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
